    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I do agree that \"chaining\" operations after yanking is not really possible, linewise textobject here makes more sense to me. This *is* what I would expect `dai` / `dii` / `cai` / `cii` do. If it is charwise, then for example `dii` would end up with a line with trailing whitespace. The actually useful case would need to be \n\nBesides, changing this behavior would be breaking, which raises a bar for its justification quite a bit.\n\nSo I am afraid this is not planned.",
